---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release } from '../lib/publication';
import { url } from '../lib/publication';
const selectedClaims = ['C-NSO-PREMISES-2018', 'C-NSO-SUFFICIENCY-2018', 'C-JJM-CONNECTIONS-20260303', 'C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024'].map(id => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id)).filter(Boolean);
---
<Site title="Water and people"><PageHeader title="Water and people" eyebrow="Population · use · access" description="More people, different uses and changed infrastructure can alter exposure. None can be reduced to one national pressure score." /><section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid"><article><h2>Three denominators to keep apart</h2><p><strong>Population</strong> counts people in a specified boundary and year. <strong>Demand</strong> is a flow over time and depends on use, price, losses and service. <strong>Access</strong> describes delivery and quality, which can vary within the same district.</p><div class="note"><strong>Latest count versus projection</strong><p>The Census of India publishes completed census tables; population projections use a model and reference date. Their lines should not be drawn as one observed series.</p></div><h2>What a tap connection does not settle</h2><p>A reported connection count documents a programme output. Quantity, continuity and quality require separate service measurements or functionality assessments. A connection should not be labelled reliable water delivery without those checks.</p><h2>Questions that need local records</h2><ul><li>Which utility or panchayat serves the place, and from which sources?</li><li>How often does supply arrive, at what volume and tested quality?</li><li>How do farming, industry and household uses vary by season?</li><li>Who pays more in money or collection time when a shared system fails?</li></ul></article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Primary source leads</p><a href="https://censusindia.gov.in/nada/index.php/catalog/6191">2011 Census table ↗</a><a href="https://www.mohfw.gov.in/sites/default/files/Population%20Projection%20Report%202011-2036%20-%20upload_compressed_0.pdf">Official population projections ↗</a><a href="https://jaljeevanmission.gov.in/functionality-report-2024">JJM functionality assessments ↗</a><a href={url('/impacts/')}>Consequences and access</a></aside></div></section><section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed, attributed source records</p><h2>Different snapshots, different denominators</h2><p>The 2018 household survey, 2026 administrative connection count and 2024 sampled functionality assessment have different populations and definitions. They are not one trend line.</p>{selectedClaims[0] && <ClaimBlock claim={selectedClaims[0]} heading="2018: facility within premises" />}{selectedClaims[1] && <ClaimBlock claim={selectedClaims[1]} heading="2018: reported year-round sufficiency" />}{selectedClaims[2] && <ClaimBlock claim={selectedClaims[2]} heading="2026: administrative connection report" />}{selectedClaims[3] && <ClaimBlock claim={selectedClaims[3]} heading="2024: sampled functionality" />}</div></section></Site>
